    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0322" n="240" xml:id="pg240"/>

                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Kanagazva,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 13, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    received a letter from the ministers for foreign affairs, in which they state
                    that they had determined not to send the embassy to the treaty powers, as
                    previously announced.</p>
                <p>In my despatch, No. 57, of the 3d September last, I informed you that the embassy
                    would not go further than Shanghai, the appointment having been made only for
                    the purpose of gaining time, by inducing the hostile party to believe that the
                    Tycoon had not abandoned the hope of obtaining from the treaty powers the
                    concession of the closing of this port.</p>
                <p>The letter of the ministers for foreign affairs is only of importance as another
                    evidence of the increased strength of the government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
